{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/79006-a-demon-s-real-name","id":79006,"title":"A Demon's 'Real Name'","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-24T19:49:29-08:00","id":79006,"title":"A Demon's 'Real Name'","content":"What would qualify as the demon's 'real name', for purposes of casting magic on them? Would it be the name they're given by the GM? The name they choose for themselves? Could angels have real names, tethered as they are to the GM's network?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>What do we want? 3rd Edition Sidereals!<br /> When do we want it? In accordance with the dictates of Fate!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/867-jimborg","name":"Jimborg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T20:59:17-08:00","id":79078,"title":"","content":"I think it's something along the lines of a GMC computer code signal which can't be pronounced verbally, but could be transmitted between Demons for Hell knows what reason, or to others telepathically, if one has the means to do so. Or perhaps it could be communicated by adding the honest intent to do so while telling someone their name using inaccurate verbal sounds, which the recipient could then use the knowledge of even while incanting inaccurate sounds. By and large, though, I think sympathetic spellcasters are simply going to have to eat their tough cookies and never know any Demon's True Name, just like they'll never be able to directly detect their lies.<br /> <br /> The way Mage uses True Names, they are an aspect of identity that needs (archmastery of) Space to be manipulated, so it could be possible that when a human's soul is ejected in the process of taking their life as a Cover, the Cover <i>might</i> keep its True Name, on account of Space being a Gross Arcanum. That would be an okay justification if a Storyteller wanted to use that dynamic for whatever technical fun they want to play with, though I would default to saying no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/486-foolish-milex","name":"Foolish Milex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T21:46:29-08:00","id":79102,"title":"","content":"I dunno, the image of binding a demon by knowing its true name is popular enough that i'd be inclined to make that a part of the game. Plus, the idea of an identifier having fundamental significance beyond just another word or sound lends itself well to the God-Machine's control over its servants.<br /> <br /> I would say that the name the GM gave them as angels would count as their true name (which probably makes a lot of demons <i>really angry</i>), and I could imagine an Embed like Identity Theft letting you 'spoof' your true name while active. That seems like the kind of thing canny Unchained would want to be on top of in a chronicle that featured mages. Angels have true names, with a note to the storyteller that the GM knows much more about the functioning of the occult concept of true names than a given mage does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T21:56:01-08:00","id":79104,"title":"","content":"Their <a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/4464486/cipherdictionarydef.png\" target=\"_blank\">Cipher</a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 02-25-2014, 01:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T12:01:11-08:00","id":84094,"title":"","content":"I think making demons names outright unknowable is too strong of an advantage against mages. Demons can use their cover dots to resist supernatural abilities, which means a fresh demon character can already roll 7 resist dice.<br /> <br /> I got 3 general ideas:<br /> 1 -- I might be conflating <i>Dresden Files</i> with <i>Mage</i>, but thought I'd read that the name of a Pattern is the whatever it calls itself. If your parents named you one thing but you were kidnapped from your crib and raised to have a different name, the one you grew up with is the one a mage needs. Applied to <i>Demon</i>, that name could be almost anything depending on what the demon considers closest to it<b>self</b>. So it might be the name they use with their rings and agencies, the piece of themselves that doesn't change with what skin they wear. It might be the name of their first cover, if it's a cover they were especially attached to. The Cipher is a super cool idea and might be true of demons who know theirs.<br /> <br /> 2 -- If you like traditional lore, Foolish Milex's suggestion is similar to what <i>World of Darkness: Inferno</i> has to say on name magic. &quot;A [demon's] Secret Name is not really a word. [...] Think of it as more of a spiritual frequency: a carrier wave that transmits the power of Hell.[...] it can be \u201cembedded\u201d into many forms of information: a spoken or written word, a series of numbers, even a picture. [...] A demonologist must still learn it, and the source must be part of a line of transmission that consists of a chain of honest renderings, moving from the source of the revelation to the student.&quot; (p.38) Here names seem to be given by superiors, so I guess they'd come from the God-Machine. Those rules go on to talk about how the sympathy of these names can become diluted if they're widely known and repeated improperly. For a God-Machine demon, you might imagine that the names are digital information and normal human communications are too analog to store them with enough accuracy after 2 or 3 recordings.<br /> <br /> 3 -- I think of greatest value would be the name a demon signs to a pact, because whatever mark they make there is one they will be genuinely bound by. They might sign as &quot;Mr. Stone&quot; or &quot;Asphodel&quot; but to make it work, they know they have to declare this link in the code of the Universe. This is likely to be whatever name they told the mortal, which might not be the same one they use on all their pacts. Now for a dramatic tradeoff: perhaps using lots of different names makes it harder for angels to trace the pacts, but any one of those names are viable conduits for a mage. I might even go so far as to say that if a mage gets a hold of a demon's soul pact, they've got the equivalent of a soulstone for sympathy purposes; after all, soul pacts are signed in blood, which is automatic Intimate sympathy at least. A demon with no pacts... is never &quot;safe&quot;... but they have no names a mage can use.<br /> <br /> Number 3 is what I'd have it be if I was running the game, since it's just an added twist on something the demon system already has.<br /> <br /> Regarding angels, I'd treat them as spirits until they Fall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1925,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1925-toroid","user":"Toroid","date":".  Fixed a typo and refined option 2 03-04-2014, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1925-toroid","name":"Toroid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T13:39:08-08:00","id":84202,"title":"","content":"I love the way Demons' true names were presented in Inferno. I love the idea that what ever name the Demon signs on its pacts is its true name. And I absolutely adore the idea that a Demon's Cipher is its true name. I don't think any if these ideas are mutually exclusive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T19:25:16-08:00","id":84332,"title":"","content":"I thought I read somewhere that God-m only gave names to the angels it was going to keep around for an extended period of time, or reuse. Anyways, considering that Demons get to use their cover as their Supernatural resistance; if I were going to run a crossover with Mages, I would use their cover as their 'True Name'. Consider that Demon's should be constantly vigilant and that would up the Paranoia a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T19:36:20-08:00","id":84335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>miss_minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/79006-a-demon-s-real-name?p=84332#post84332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought I read somewhere that God-m only gave names to the angels it was going to keep around for an extended period of time, or reuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Close, but not quite.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>&quot;Names,&quot; DtD Core pg 91, sidebar</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The God-Machine only gives angels names when they will need to identify themselves. Angels tasked with working among teams of loyalists or travelling to far-off facilities have strange, often unpronounceable designation \u201cnames\u201d closer to strings of characters or bursts of computer code than language. Angels tasked with identifying themselves as supernatural beings to humans sometimes have more classical \u201cangelic\u201d names like Barachiel or Haniel, arrived at by translating a description of their purpose and \u201cof God\u201d into Hebrew.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T20:11:54-08:00","id":84348,"title":"","content":"Oh that's where I got confused; I kinda meshed the two. See, I just can't be expected to remember anything without a tangible book to carry around and consult. That doesn't chance my stance though. I'd just go with their Cover's name. If I had five covers and a Mage discovered that I was the Demon once Angel Conflarel with a Mage's awesome powers all of my covers would basically be compromised (Not in the D:tD sense of the word though). While I just adore everything about Mage, they shouldn't be allowed to curb stomp every other splat. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T09:30:38-08:00","id":86067,"title":"","content":"They don't have them. A demon is unaffected by magic that relies on &quot;True Names.&quot;<br /> <br /> Why? Because a demon's &quot;true name&quot; is whatever the demon wants it to be. She is her demonic self, and all of her Covers, at once. (Does that mean if she's Burned, she only has one name? Maybe! Sounds like a great story hook!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T23:35:01-08:00","id":86527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/79006-a-demon-s-real-name?p=86067#post86067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't have them. A demon is unaffected by magic that relies on &quot;True Names.&quot;<br /> <br /> Why? Because a demon's &quot;true name&quot; is whatever the demon wants it to be. She is her demonic self, and all of her Covers, at once. (Does that mean if she's Burned, she only has one name? Maybe! Sounds like a great story hook!)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's implication of <b>Liar's Tongue</b> ( DtD p.183 ) of demons? That they <b>choose</b>, what is true to them?<br /> <br /> If so, what with summoning? Let's say my mage was confronted with God-Machine and somehow he knows about demons ( from Mysterium Atheneum probably <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). He want's to confront with one of it's angels or demons at least. What would he proposed to summon them rituals like in <b>Inferno</b>, with Name chosen by his image of demon? Who the answer to it - any demon that want's, one that is closest to &quot;description&quot;, any other combination?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T07:25:27-08:00","id":86743,"title":"","content":"You can't summon the Unchained like you would spirits, because they aren't spirits anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}